# Kiosk chrome vs everything else

Home and garden serve the same frontend. **Kiosk-visible chrome** (layout,
CSS, clock, fullscreen, LYS/SOL/cards the tablets show) that only lands on
one Pi leaves the other on old UI.

**Do both hubs + `Page.reload` only then.** Say why in one sentence.

**Do not** reload kiosks for iPhone/PWA icons, favicon, manifest, service
worker, or docs. Put those files on the hub the phone actually hits
(usually garden). Skip a site whose kiosk heartbeat says ADB is dead;
say so instead of discovering it with `adb connect`.

Use `scripts/hubctl` for status, static sync, backend copy, and reload.
Do not rediscover vault passwords or CDP. Detect the Mac LAN first
(`site-location`). Simon looks; no Cursor browser QA.

## Deploy gate

`hubctl static` and `hubctl backend` refuse a dirty working tree, a HEAD that
is not `origin/main`, and a page whose baked commit is not an ancestor of HEAD.

`hubctl backend` uploads Python only. It does not copy `backend/static` and it
does not write `static-id`. The live page is `/home/simmoe/HUE_EJDERSTED/served`,
which a backend copy cannot reach.

`hubctl static` builds into a fresh directory from that commit, stamps the sha
into `index.html` and `build-id`, and writes `static-id` only after the Pi's
`build-id` matches HEAD. It never uploads the checkout's `backend/static`.

Do not scp `backend/`, `backend/static`, or `served` by hand. If the command
refuses, commit, push, and merge until this checkout contains the page's commit.
Then run hubctl again.
